course: dictionary
lesson: 5592
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can mean more than one thing, so context tells you which meaning fits. A library is most often a place with books. «Borrowing books from the public library is free, and a parent can help you get your own library card.» The words borrowing and card are clues that this library is a place where you take books home.
explain: Some words sound clear but need care. «If a library book is damaged, you tell the librarian when you return it.» Here library book means a book that belongs to a library and is lent out. Swap in your meaning: a book that belongs to a library still makes sense, so you have picked the right one.
explain: The clues show the meaning. Ask: where am I, and what am I doing there? Borrowing and returning point to a library that lends books. A room in a school where books are kept, or a set of code in computing, would not fit these clues. Try your meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: A library is a place with many books, and often films and computers, that people can borrow or use.
fact: A library can also be a room in a school or house where books are kept.
fact: A library can be a collection of books, music or games that someone owns.
fact: In computing, a library is a set of ready-made code.
fact: When you borrow a library book it is taken off the shelf, and when you return it, it goes back on the shelf.
exercise: In «Borrowing books from the public library is free», what kind of place is a library? | A kind of computer game | A room where people cook | *A place with many books that people can borrow | A shop that sells books
exercise: A library has 4 shelves with 12 books on each shelf. How many books are there in total? | *48 | 16 | 42 | 36
exercise: A library has 20 books on its shelves. Ella borrows 5 and later returns 2. How many books are on the shelves now? | 15 | 23 | 13 | *17
test: A parent can help you get your own library card. What does this tell you about a library? | It is a collection of games someone owns | It is a shelf in a shop | *It is a place where people borrow books | It is a set of ready-made code
test: In computing, what is a library? | A type of library fine | A card with a due date on it | *A set of ready-made code | A pile of old newspapers
exam: Why is it better to tell the librarian about a damaged or lost library book than to hide it? | A lost book is never a problem | Telling the librarian means you must pay twice | *Hiding it is worse than paying for it | Hiding it makes the library bigger
